    "['delete set protocols [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'undo mpls lsr-id', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'undo mpls lsr-id', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nundo mpls lsr-id\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Huawei devices, the equivalent of deleting MPLS configuration (which would remove the MPLS base configuration) is typically done by removing the LSR ID, as MPLS cannot function without an LSR ID. The Juniper `delete set protocols mpls` command removes all MPLS protocol configuration, and the closest Huawei equivalent is to undo the MPLS LSR ID, which effectively disables MPLS functionality. If there are other MPLS-specific configurations (like interfaces), they would need to be removed separately.', 'trans_template': 'undo mpls lsr-id'}]]": 1,
