Back0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. \"mpls ldp\" enables LDP globally (equivalent to \"set protocols ldp\")\\n2. The interface commands enable LDP on specific interfaces\\n3. The router-id command sets the LDP router ID using the loopback interface\\n4. Note that HUAWEI uses different interface naming (GigabitEthernet instead of ge)\\n5. The \".0\" subinterface notation is not needed in HUAWEI\\'s basic LDP configuration', 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/4'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'mpls ldp router-id LoopBack0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'mpls ldp router-id LoopBack0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent HUAWEI configuration for the Juniper LDP commands:\\n\\n##\\nmpls ldp\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/3\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/4\\nmpls ldp router-id LoopBack0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. \"mpls ldp\" enables LDP globally (equivalent to \"set protocols ldp\")\\n2. The interface commands enable LDP on specific interfaces\\n3. The router-id command sets the LDP router ID using the loopback interface\\n4. Note that HUAWEI uses different interface naming (GigabitEthernet instead of ge)\\n5. The \".0\" subinterface notation is not needed in HUAWEI\\'s basic LDP configuration', 'trans_template': 'mpls ldp router-id LoopBack0'}]]": 1,
